1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,944
The seller gave Jason a name to trust.
Lucia found it on a memorial before

2
00:00:05,944 --> 00:00:06,340
paying.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:11,890
They had left a deposit with the clerk
for a boat neither had seen.

4
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:17,446
Their seller claimed the owner was away.
He said the key and title would

5
00:00:17,446 --> 00:00:19,430
arrive after the final payment.

6
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:24,579
Lucia walked beneath the dock shelter to
escape the rain. The same name

7
00:00:24,579 --> 00:00:26,560
shone on a brass plaque.

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:31,717
The owner had died last winter. His boat
had become a community rescue

9
00:00:31,717 --> 00:00:33,700
launch. It wasn't for sale.

10
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:38,849
Jason called the seller. This time, the
phone rang inside an empty tackle

11
00:00:38,849 --> 00:00:40,830
shop and nobody answered it.

12
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:45,586
They took their receipt back to the
clerk. She checked the listing,

13
00:00:45,586 --> 00:00:48,360
returned their deposit, and reported the
impersonation.

14
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:52,604
Outside, the rescue launch crossed the
channel. Jason watched their

15
00:00:52,604 --> 00:00:56,000
imaginary getaway boat bring somebody
safely home instead.
